From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mouyase <mouyase@example.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:26:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] NX1: empty lineage.dependencies, resolution is in the local
 manifest

lineage.dependencies pins three repos by name with no revision. When
'breakfast NX1' runs, roomservice resolves those names against the
LineageOS upstream manifest, so sepolicy_vndr and hardware_mediatek get
checked out from LineageOS instead of the Bluefox forks. The upstream
repos have no MT6768 support, so the build fails on missing MTK HALs.

Both Bluefox forks do have lineage-24.0 branches, but roomservice has no
way to know to use them. All three dependencies are now declared with
explicit revisions in .repo/local_manifests/nx1.xml, making this file
redundant. Leaving it non-empty actively causes a second conflicting
checkout attempt, so it is reduced to an empty array that breakfast can
still parse.
---
 device/bluefox/NX1/lineage.dependencies | 16 +---------------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/device/bluefox/NX1/lineage.dependencies b/device/bluefox/NX1/lineage.dependencies
index 1764468..fe51488 100644
--- a/device/bluefox/NX1/lineage.dependencies
+++ b/device/bluefox/NX1/lineage.dependencies
@@ -1,15 +1 @@
-[
-  {
-    "repository": "android_device_bluefox_NX1-kernels",
-    "target_path": "device/bluefox/NX1-kernels",
-    "remote": "github"
-  },
-  {
-    "repository": "android_device_mediatek_sepolicy_vndr",
-    "target_path": "device/mediatek/sepolicy_vndr"
-  },
-  {
-    "repository": "android_hardware_mediatek",
-    "target_path": "hardware/mediatek"
-  }
-]
+[]
